year: 2026
license: MIT
keywords:
  - HIV-2
  - protease inhibitor resistance
  - cross-species transfer learning
  - drug resistance prediction
  - machine learning
  - biophysical features
  - clinical validation
repository-code: "https://github.com/nunnajaswant-ship-it/HIV-2_DRUG_RESISTANCE_TRANFER_LEARNING_ON_HIV-1"
abstract: >-
  A machine-learning framework for HIV-2 protease-inhibitor resistance prediction built by
  cross-species transfer learning from HIV-1. The model is pre-trained on 5,683 curated HIV-1
  phenotypic assays, applied zero-shot to HIV-2, and fine-tuned on a 160-row HIV-2 ChEMBL panel.
  On measured HIV-2 binding affinities it significantly outperforms a Stanford-derived rule-based
  interpretation (R = 0.7018 vs 0.4724; delta-R = +0.229; P <= 0.001), and it recovers a positive,
  drug-dependent signal on 2,616 never-seen HIV-2 clinical rows without any clinical label
  entering training.
